==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 60~73.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Bore]]s spawn after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>, delay 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]] spawns as the boss.
*Infinite [[Shy Boy]]s spawn after 920 seconds<sup>27,600f</sup>, delay 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Be prepared for a long, long battle. Unless you've beaten [[Into the Future]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cat]] will likely be among your only attackers that can reasonably hit Crazed Bird Cat; and while the Bores can be beaten by spamming [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cats]], the challenge comes from not losing too much money or ground in doing so. You can also use units such as [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] to inflict CC on the Bore to not lose ground that way. Spammable ranged attackers (such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]]) work best against the Rain Ds, and [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]] helps against everything but the boss. [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] is a lifesaver, simultaneously damaging Crazed Bird Cat and helping you regain lost ground.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]] - An absolute must-have for this stage, with its cheap price and good stats for the cost, it can tank Crazed Bird and deal some nice damage to it over time, and more importantly, handle Bore. It cannot deal with Rain D. effectively however.

*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] - Sporting high stats for the cost and powerful attacks, it can help deal with Bore and Crazed Bird itself similarly to Crazed Fish, and has the capability to slow down Bores. Like CFish, however, he has low range.

*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] - Useful for both stalling the boss and allowing other units to take more hits, however its low range leads it to die from Rain D. very quickly.

*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - At the point you're able to get this unit, this unit easily trivializes the stage with its Slow ability and insanely high range, can help knock back the [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]], providing excellent crowd control.

*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]] - Their fast speeds allow you to keep the Crazed Bird at a hold if you send them out continuously, they must be accompanied by hard hitting units alongside them. A level 20 Crazed Wall Cat can survive a hit from Crazed Bird Cat, allowing you to stall it very effectively.

In the event that you have cleared Into the Future, just sending out one [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] at the right time can already drain almost 50% of Crazed Bird Cat's health.

